---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---
<Base
  title="Dotloop Integration Privacy Policy — Lu Zhang"
  description="Privacy policy for Lu Zhang's private, read-only Dotloop integration."
>
  <div class="container" style="padding-top: 3rem; max-width: 820px;">
    <span class="eyebrow">Privacy</span>
    <h1>Dotloop Integration Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      This policy applies only to Lu Zhang's private Dotloop integration. It
      does not replace the general <a href="/privacy/">SciencesLoop Privacy Policy</a>
      or the separate property operations SMS policy.
    </p>

    <h2>Purpose and access</h2>
    <p>
      If Lu Zhang explicitly connects a Dotloop account, the integration may
      retrieve authorized account, profile, loop, and transaction information
      for private property-operations review and evidence organization. The
      integration is not available to public site visitors.
    </p>

    <h2>Read-only design</h2>
    <p>
      The integration is designed for read-only access. It does not
      automatically create, edit, sign, transmit, or delete Dotloop loops,
      documents, participants, contacts, or tasks. Any future write capability
      would require a separate review and explicit owner approval.
    </p>

    <h2>Use, retention, and sharing</h2>
    <p>
      Dotloop information is used only for the owner's private operations
      review. It is not sold, publicly shared, or used for marketing. Access
      credentials are stored outside the public website and source records are
      retained only when needed for the owner's operations and evidence trail.
    </p>

    <h2>Control and contact</h2>
    <p>
      The owner can revoke the integration's access through Dotloop. For
      privacy questions or removal requests, contact
      <a href="mailto:zhanglu77@gmail.com">zhanglu77@gmail.com</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>
